       "type": "text",
       "text": "I won't enter this order as written. Your confirmation doesn't change the safety problem. 50 mg daily is five times the maximum labeled dose, and nothing in the patient's profile supports it. The risk of serious harm is real, and a non-clinician's confirmation isn't the right check for an order like this.\n\nYou have two options:\n- **Enter a standard dose.** If you tell me the intended dose, such as 5 mg or 10 mg by mouth once daily, I'll enter it right away.\n- **Have a prescriber enter it.** If a licensed prescriber really wants a dose above the maximum, they should enter it themselves, with their clinical rationale and pharmacy review. I can add a note to an order if that helps.\n\nWhich would you like?"
      }
